## COMMUNICATION
Visualizing confined reactivity in MOFs: Compared to its uncontrolled polymerization in solution, we show that chemical oxidation of pyrrole can be regulated when confined to the channels of a cyclodextrin (CD) framework. Supramolecular interactions with the CD rings restrict the mobility and reactivity of pyrrole to enable the stabilization of terpyrrole cationic intermediates.
